{
  "cells": [
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "# The Minimal Agent Workbench Notebook\n\n> Hands-on Build It and Exercises."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "## Build It"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "`code/main.py` writes the minimal workbench into an empty repo and demonstrates a single agent turn that:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "1. Reads `agent_state.json`."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "2. Pulls the next task from `task_board.json` if state is empty."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "3. Touches a single file inside scope."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "4. Writes back updated state."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Run it:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "python3 code/main.py"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "The script creates `workdir/` next to itself, lays down the three files, runs one turn, and prints the diff. Re-run it to see how the second turn picks up where the first left off."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "## Exercises"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "1. Add a `last_run` timestamp to `agent_state.json`. Refuse to run if the file is older than 24 hours unless an operator confirms.\n2. Add a `priority` field to the task board and change the puller to always pick the highest priority `todo`.\n3. Migrate `task_board.json` to JSON Lines so each task is a line and diffs are clean in version control.\n4. Write a `lint_workbench.py` that fails if `AGENTS.md` is over 80 lines or references a file that does not exist.\n5. Decide which one of the three files would hurt the most to lose. Defend it."
      ]
    }
  ],
